---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Badge } from '@highjack/ui';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The game — HighJack"
  description="What HighJack can play today: a private match with dice, property, rent, tax and bankruptcy, decided by an authoritative server."
>
  <header class="border-b border-line-subtle pb-12">
    <p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-500">Playable now</p>
    <h1 class="mb-0 mt-4 font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl">What you can play</h1>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      The current release is the core board loop. Create a private match, share its id, and take
      turns rolling, buying and paying rent. The server decides every outcome.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="border-b border-line-subtle py-14" aria-labelledby="turn-title">
    <h2 id="turn-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl text-cream-100 sm:text-3xl">
      How a turn works
    </h2>
    <ol class="mt-8 grid list-none gap-10 p-0 md:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="border-t border-line-subtle pt-5">
        <p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs text-gold-500">01</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-cream-100">You act</h3>
        <p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Roll the dice, then choose to buy or decline the property you land on. End the turn when
          you are done.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="border-t border-line-subtle pt-5">
        <p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs text-gold-500">02</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-cream-100">
          The server decides
        </h3>
        <p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          It applies your action, charges rent, awards bonuses and advances the turn. Your browser
          receives the result and draws it.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-line-subtle py-14" aria-labelledby="authority-title">
    <h2 id="authority-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl text-cream-100 sm:text-3xl">
      Who decides what happens
    </h2>
    <div
      class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto border-l-2 border-l-gold-500 py-2 pl-6"
      tabindex={0}
      aria-label="Action flow diagram, scrollable"
    >
      <pre class="m-0 min-w-[28rem] font-mono text-xs leading-loose text-muted-400 sm:text-sm"><code>Your choice
    ↓
Action sent to the server
    ↓
Engine applies one transition
    ↓
Events describe what changed
    ↓
Every player sees the same state</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      The browser only requests and renders. Rolls come from a seeded stream, so the same seed and
      the same actions reproduce the same match.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-l-2 border-l-gold-500 py-2 pl-6 my-14" aria-label="Development status">
    <h2 class="m-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-cream-100">
      Current status
      <Badge tone="gold">Playable</Badge>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 mb-0 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      Two to eight players can join one private match. The board loop covers dice, movement,
      buying, rent, tax, bankruptcy and victory. The client is a Solid app over a canvas board; it
      renders server state and does not compute outcomes. Run it locally with:
      <code class="ml-1 rounded bg-felt-800 px-2 py-1 font-mono text-xs text-gold-400">
        bun run dev:game
      </code>
    </p>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      Trading, auctions and the other systems are not playable yet. Their status is listed on the
      <a class="text-gold-400 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-cream-100" href="/features"
        >features page</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
